摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Multi-agent orchestration and LLM model routing for DeepSeek Harness (DSH): semantic AI agent profiles, exact model routes, declarative teams and strategies, and bounded subagent delegation - a TypeScript plugin that adds no second runtime.","id":"gh:1334005699","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-legion","slug":"wxxb789/dsh-legion","topics":["agent-client-protocol","agent-orchestration","agentic-ai","ai-agents","claude-code","codex","coding-agent","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","llm-orchestration","llm-routing","model-routing","multi-agent","multi-agent-systems","orchestration","subagents"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Multi-agent orchestration and LLM model routing for DeepSeek Harness (DSH): semantic AI agent profil"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"es, exact model routes, declarative teams and strategies, and bounded subagent delegation - a TypeSc"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ript plugin that adds no second runtime."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-legion: Multi-Agent Orchestration and LLM Model Routing for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**dsh-legion** is a TypeScript multi-agent orchestration plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). It turns"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" one AI coding agent into a bounded orchestration cohort: configurable AI agent Specialists, an exac"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"t LLM model router, declarative Cohorts and Strategies, structured results, and depth-limited subage"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"nt delegation — without replacing the DSH runtime."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What is dsh-legion used for?"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Legion is useful when one AI coding agent should delegate different kinds of work under explicit, re"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ul when one AI coding agent should delegate different kinds of work under explicit, reusable policy."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Route work by task type.** Send extraction or summaries to a fast model and architecture or debu"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"gging to a deeper model.\n- **Run independent reviews.** Give a reviewer read-only tools, a separate "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"persona, and a structured `review-v1` result.\n- **Build multi-agent workflows.** Define bounded Coho"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"rts and declarative plan/execute/review or research fanout Strategies.\n- **Bound workload and risk.*"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"* Limit depth, concurrency, participants, deadlines, output size, tools, and eligible routes. These "},{"id":"p7s6","text":"bounds constrain cost drivers, but Legion does not provide aggregate token or monetary-cost admissio"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"n.\n- **Standardize delegation.** Keep semantic Specialist names stable when the underlying model or "},{"id":"p7s8","text":"backend changes.\n- **Validate policy before runtime.** Diagnose configuration against explicit provi"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"der capability fixtures.\n- **Customize without forking.** Add, replace, disable, or revive Specialis"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"ts, Cohorts, and Strategies through Catalog Layers."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Legion is for developers and deployment owners who already use DSH and want configurable multi-agent"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" delegation without adopting another scheduler, session store, or agent runtime."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Capabilities"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Capability | What it provides |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Semantic Specialists | Named policies such as `quick`, `deep`, and `review` instead of raw model c"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"hoices in every prompt. |\n| Exact model routing | Up to eight ordered provider/model candidates with"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" static context and output-budget constraints. |\n| Multiple backends | Use `spawn`, `fork`, `codex`,"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" `claude-code`, or another DSH-registered subagent provider per Specialist. |\n| Tool and persona pol"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"icy | Restrict child tools, add Specialist instructions, set depth, and choose foreground/background"},{"id":"p11s6","text":" defaults. |\n| Structured results | Versioned `text`, `findings-v1`, and `review-v1` foreground resu"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"lt contracts. |\n| Custom Cohorts | Declare bounded Member Slots that reference existing Specialists."},{"id":"p11s8","text":" |\n| Declarative Strategies | Compile typed artifact graphs to frozen DSH delegation primitives. |\n["},{"id":"p11s9","text":"clarative Strategies | Compile typed artifact graphs to frozen DSH delegation primitives. |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- A compatible DeepSeek Harness installation.\n- `pnpm` on `PATH`; `dsh plugin` forwards package oper"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ations to pnpm.\n- A DSH Host `profile`, such as the default `web` composition.\n- A configured DSH su"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"bagent provider and the LLM provider/model routes referenced by your Specialists.\n- For local develo"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"pment: Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0` and pnpm `11.21.0`."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Status and limitations"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The source tree declares version `1.2.0`; canonical current configuration is v3, while published 1.x"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" no-target materialization/export remains v2 for compatibility. Check CHANGELOG.md, the roadmap, and"},{"id":"p15s3","text":" GitHub Releases before selecting or upgrading an install revision."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Known limitations:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Curated Strategies are not automatically model-exposed; deployment owners may opt in with `enableS"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"trategies: true`.\n- DSH has no unified recovery owner across provider retries and Route Candidates, "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"so Legion starts only the selected child and never retries or switches models after failure.\n- DSH b"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"inds a prepared call to one adapter generation and one dispatch, but Legion's pre-start Route observ"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"ations are point-in-time, best-effort facts rather than an atomic adapter-topology snapshot.\n- A Spe"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"cialist cannot override a child's reasoning effort.\n- In-process children inherit the parent's named"},{"id":"p17s7","text":" DSH agent preset; no per-child named preset or Specialist-local DSH Skill setup is available across"},{"id":"p17s8","text":" one-shot, continuable, and cold-resume paths. Specialists can still vary model, persona, tools, bac"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"kend, and limits.\n- Legion does not inspect live provider health, credentials, authorization, quota,"},{"id":"p17s10","text":" reachability, or latency; Route Plans report those facts as unknown.\n- Aggregate token or monetary-"},{"id":"p17s11","text":"cost admission remains a future Host-owned capability; it is unrelated to the observation-only Run R"},{"id":"p17s12","text":"eceipt companion. Current limits cover members, concurrency, deadlines, accepted output, tools, and "},{"id":"p17s13","text":"eligible routes.\n- The GUI settings card edits five scalar policies; Specialists, Cohorts, Strategie"},{"id":"p17s14","text":"s, and catalog layers stay in the configuration document.\n- DSH now publishes assessed-line client c"},{"id":"p17s15","text":"ontracts, including the `settings.plugin.item` slot declaration, but not its `clientBundle` build pr"},{"id":"p17s16","text":"eset. Legion therefore typechecks against public packages while reproducing the loader artifact form"},{"id":"p17s17","text":"at by hand; a Host format change fails at load time rather than at build time.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Compatibility, development, and releases"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"The package requires Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0` and the DSH peer range declared in `contracts/co"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"mpatibility.json`. Legion tracks the assessed Host line from that single policy: the package peer ra"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"nge, declared minimum, latest tested version, CI channels, and packed verifier are checked against i"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"t rather than copying version literals. CI covers Windows, Ubuntu, packed DSH consumers, public cont"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"racts, protocol benchmarks, and reproducible packages."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Useful references:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- Implementation roadmap\n- Public contract v1\n- Durable Strategy Runs\n- Journal contract v1\n- Run re"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"play\n- Run Receipts\n- Versioned configuration and rollback\n- Declarative Cohort and Strategy IR\n- Ex"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"plicit Strategy exposure authority\n- Reproducible releases\n- All architecture decisions"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Issues and contributions are welcome through the GitHub issue tracker."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
